        "title": "Comparative Physiology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Comparative physiology uses the diversity of animal designs to understand the physics and chemistry of biological function. Every major organ system has been solved differently by different phyla — sometimes convergently (independent origins of the eye, closed circulatory system), sometimes divergently (different solutions to the same problem: gas exchange across gill, lung, trachea, skin). The comparative approach reveals what is physically necessary vs what is historically contingent."
    },
